{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00069",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.27,
      "end_seconds": 3.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Hello doctor, sorry, am I early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.47,
      "end_seconds": 7.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Yes, do sit. Tell me what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.91,
      "end_seconds": 19.15,
      "duration_seconds": 10.24,
      "text": "It's pain low in the pelvis. I thought I'd wait, um, but it hasn't gone. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.58,
      "end_seconds": 23.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.03,
      "end_seconds": 27.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Um, it's been going on for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.84,
      "end_seconds": 33.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Okay, is it constant, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.34,
      "end_seconds": 37.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "It happens a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.57,
      "end_seconds": 39.53,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Anything that helps?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.33,
      "end_seconds": 42.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "A hot water bottle helps a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.41,
      "end_seconds": 47.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Go on. Okay, how would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.39,
      "end_seconds": 49.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "It's mild, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.03,
      "end_seconds": 56.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Have you had any vaginal discharge or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.5,
      "end_seconds": 60.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "No vaginal discharge or vomiting, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.46,
      "end_seconds": 68.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.12,
      "end_seconds": 76.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Heart disease, for five years. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.87,
      "end_seconds": 81.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Right. Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.27,
      "end_seconds": 84.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.18,
      "end_seconds": 86.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.71,
      "end_seconds": 89.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.52,
      "end_seconds": 94.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.43,
      "end_seconds": 108.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.39,
      "end_seconds": 115.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.35,
      "end_seconds": 119.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.81,
      "end_seconds": 123.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.03,
      "end_seconds": 126.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.55,
      "end_seconds": 130.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.66,
      "end_seconds": 141.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.4,
      "text": "I'm, I'm on aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day for my heart. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.38,
      "end_seconds": 155.32,
      "duration_seconds": 13.94,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.79,
      "end_seconds": 158.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.9,
      "end_seconds": 163.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.77,
      "end_seconds": 164.59,
      "duration_seconds": 0.82,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.1,
      "end_seconds": 182.82,
      "duration_seconds": 10.72,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. From what you've told me, it fits best with chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.66,
      "end_seconds": 185.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.77,
      "end_seconds": 201.53,
      "duration_seconds": 14.76,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with chronic pelvic pain, possibly endometriosis do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain low in the pelvis for three weeks, mild, and no vomiting or vaginal discharge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.15,
      "end_seconds": 207.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.81,
      "end_seconds": 210.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.09,
      "end_seconds": 211.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.4,
      "end_seconds": 240.89,
      "duration_seconds": 15.49,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. We should do a pelvic ultrasound for pelvic pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. I'd like you to take mefenamic acid, 500 milligrams, three times a day with food, for five days. That's for period pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.89,
      "end_seconds": 245.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Okay, and I take that after food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.73,
      "end_seconds": 257.5,
      "duration_seconds": 11.77,
      "text": "A heat pad and some gentle movement help many people, and a pain diary helps me see a pattern. I'd like you to see a gynaecologist as well, and I'll write the referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.69,
      "end_seconds": 260.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Alright, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.04,
      "end_seconds": 269.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the pain becomes sudden and severe or you faint, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.46,
      "end_seconds": 275.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.26,
      "end_seconds": 278.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Let's review you after the scan."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.84,
      "end_seconds": 282.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.97,
      "end_seconds": 289.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "Alright, I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.38,
      "end_seconds": 300.9,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "So, I take the mefenamic acid, 500 milligrams, three times a day with food and come back after the scan. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.32,
      "end_seconds": 307.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's all I have. Is there anything you wanted to ask?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.32,
      "end_seconds": 311.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}